  "name": "SecOps — Triage Agent (tool)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Triage Agent (sub-workflow tool)\nCalled by the SecOps Orchestrator. Takes an alert (type / indicator / source), enriches with read-only security tools, grounds severity in IR runbooks (RAG), and returns a structured verdict.\n\n**Inputs:** alert_type, indicator, source\n**Output:** { verdict, severity, iocs, rationale, recommended_actions }",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky_a",
      "name": "Sticky: About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -640,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "workflowInputs": {
          "values": [
            {
              "name": "alert_type"
            },
            {
              "name": "indicator"
            },
            {
              "name": "source"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "trigger_a",
      "name": "When called by orchestrator",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -160,
        80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Triage this security alert.\n\nType: {{ $json.alert_type }}\nIndicator: {{ $json.indicator }}\nSource: {{ $json.source }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a SOC Tier-1 triage analyst. Investigate the alert's indicator using your tools: scan URLs with urlscan.io, look up indicators in MISP threat intel, and consult the incident-response runbooks (search_runbooks) for the correct procedure and severity guidance. Then return a structured triage verdict. Be conservative: if evidence is limited or mixed, mark 'suspicious' rather than 'benign'. Base severity and recommended actions on the runbooks where possible, and cite which runbook you used in the rationale."
        }
      },
